libdbus treats a process as setuid when issetugid() says so, and ignores
DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS and XDG_RUNTIME_DIR in it. llvm-libc's issetugid()
reports AT_SECURE, which Linux also sets for binaries with file
capabilities, so kwin_wayland (cap_sys_nice) could not find the session
bus. glibc has no issetugid, and there libdbus compares the real and
effective IDs instead; this makes it do the same here.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -675,7 +675,6 @@ check_functions = [
     'getresuid',
     'getrlimit',
     'inotify_init1',
-    'issetugid',
     'localeconv',
     'nanosleep',
     'pipe2',
